{"chunk_id": "3cd3b56807be", "text": "After hearing of Parashurama\u2019s destruction of the Kshatriyas, Yudhishthira marvels at the righteousness of such a feat accomplished by a Brahmana. Krishna and the Pandavas then travel to the sacred riverside where Bhishma lies upon his bed of arrows, surrounded by sages. The scene is solemn and luminous, with Bhishma resembling a fading sun. Krishna addresses the dying grandsire with deep respect, praising his mastery over death, vast knowledge of dharma, and unmatched virtue, and urging him to instruct the grieving Yudhishthira. Bhishma, raising his head, responds by offering reverent salutations to Krishna, acknowledging him as the cosmic source and dissolution of the universe\u2014marking the beginning of Bhishma\u2019s great teachings on duty and kingship.\nKrishna and the Pandavas visit Bhishma on his bed of arrows, where Krishna praises Bhishma\u2019s wisdom and asks him to instruct grieving Yudhishthira.\nThemes: reverence for Bhishma, wisdom before death, kingship and duty, divine praise, aftermath of war", "vector": [0.006374283228069544, -0.016866115853190422, -0.00019744358723983169, 0.012728770263493061, -0.005549453664571047, 0.030274545773863792, -0.015150469727814198, -0.011039519682526588, -0.015585980378091335, -0.01185115147382021, 0.016892509534955025, 0.007608228363096714, -0.0005864538252353668, 0.013217069208621979, -0.007984350435435772, -0.008492445573210716, 0.04225767031311989, 0.0040779574774205685, 0.044184472411870956, -0.02404543198645115, 0.005288807209581137, -0.007185915485024452, -0.00043880933662876487, 0.015242851339280605, -0.018278224393725395, 0.020666930824518204, 0.01627223752439022, -0.013804348185658455, -0.0019020570907741785, -0.0188984964042902, -0.014187068678438663, 0.0006648126291111112, -0.003972379490733147, 0.004011970944702625, -0.024942846968770027, -0.0017156455432996154, -0.006493058521300554, -0.010425846092402935, 0.013698769733309746, -0.007931561209261417, -0.00234